// source-numeric-draft descriptor (PLAN-961).
//
// Machine-readable contract consumed by experimental/ac-core/src/descriptor.rs.
// Superset of source-closures-draft (PLAN-865): adds the numeric surface —
// the i8/u8/u32/i64/u64/f32/f64 type kinds, typed numeric binary ops
// (`{op}_{ty}`, 107 names; i32 arithmetic keeps its frozen legacy names),
// typed negation (neg_i8/i64/f32/f64), the typed `constant` payload words
// (suffixed values) and the `cast` expression. Semantics frozen by the
// PLAN-961 T-01 contract (same-type operands, checked narrowing, IEEE
// floats, shift-amount bounds). Everything below inherits the closures
// vocabulary verbatim (records/text/collections/closures surfaces); the
// lowering reuses the 961-extended MIR instruction set.
//
// The root identity (schema/revision/profile) must be echoed by every
// accepted HIR document; unknown tags, fields, enum cases and capabilities
// are rejected. Documents under earlier identities keep their own schemas
// — profiles stay isolated by descriptor, verifier entry and canonical
// writer.

